{"id": "q_the_city_council_2", "question": "Who speaks for the wizards on the council, and what's his angle on the cult?", "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright speaks for the wizards, and he takes a hardline, proactive stance—he views the cult’s magic as a perversion and wants to use arcane tools and a possible lockdown to detect and eliminate it.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright (a gnome and Head of the Wizard’s College) is the council’s arcane representative. His angle on the cult is strongly interventionist:  \n- He views the corrupted meat and the cult’s magic as a perversion of magic itself (CANON).  \n- He is eager to deploy the Wizard’s College’s resources to detect and counteract the cult’s influence (OBSERVED).  \n- His concrete plans include using magical runes to identify corruption and proposing a magical lockdown of the city to contain the threat (OBSERVED).  \n- He takes the threat very seriously and pushes for swift, system-wide arcane solutions rather than subtle or purely political approaches (CANON + OBSERVED).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Representative of the Arcane; Head of the Wizard’s College  \n- Faction: Wizard’s College  \n- Goals: Magical detection of corruption, city lockdown, aggressive countermeasures  \n- Attitude toward cult: Sees it as dangerous, corrupt magic that must be rooted out decisively", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 732, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 23, "top_5": [["ent_the_cult", 2.5599], ["ent_city_council", 2.4199], ["ent_grobnok_the_goblin", 2.2285], ["ent_wizards_college", 2.22], ["ent_barin", 1.8885]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_the_cult", "ent_city_council", "ent_grobnok_the_goblin", "ent_wizards_college", "ent_barin", "ent_ancient_wards", "ent_commander_elric_vane", "ent_guard", "ent_magical_runes", "ent_wizards_college_detection_spell", "ent_wizards_tower_basement", "ent_wizards_meat_detection_spell", "ent_political_intrigue_among_the_council", "ent_hi