{"id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_1", "question": "When the council-chamber fight ends, where does that leave the Wolf-dead, fled, what?", "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead—**“Decapitated; head removed from body”**—with Bonogo having **“Removed the Wolf’s head to transport it.”**\n\nThere are conflicting OBSERVED states showing The Wolf attempting escape (invisibility, fleeing via the secret tunnel), but the later, decisive outcome is his death. The presence of **“Decapitated; head removed from body”** and Bonogo’s follow-up action **“Removed the Wolf’s head to transport it”** indicate this is the final, current state, overriding earlier escape attempts.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Status: Dead (decapitated)\n- Body: Separated; head taken by Bonogo\n- Prior state (overridden): Invisible and attempting escape via secret passage\n- Role in scene: Central adversary in the council chamber battle, now neutralized\n\nSo when the fight resolves, The Wolf is not at large—he’s been killed and physically removed in part from the scene.", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 732, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 24, "top_5": [["ent_arcane_locks", 1.8], ["ent_the_wolf", 1.791], ["ent_branching_paths_after_the_fight", 1.7273], ["ent_magic_pulse_alarms", 1.689], ["ent_battle_with_the_wolf_in_the_council_chamber", 1.6]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_arcane_locks", "ent_the_wolf", "ent_branching_paths_after_the_fight", "ent_magic_pulse_alarms", "ent_battle_with_the_wolf_in_the_council_chamber", "ent_doors_lock_magically", "ent_speak_with_dead", "ent_escape_tunnel", "ent_dead_horse", "ent_citizenry", "ent_magical_alarm_system", "ent_fight", "ent_city_council", "ent_the_wolfs_escape", "ent_corrupted_guard_patrol", "ent_thalia", "ent_the_city", "ent_heavy_iron_shutters", "ent_grobnok_the_goblin", "ent_necromancer", "ent_players", "ent_guards", "ent_the_wolfs_head", "ent_guard", "ent_amulets_of_coun