{"id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_2", "question": "What does the council room itself throw at us that screws with the fight?", "answer": "TL;DR: The **Council Chambers** actively interfere via **activated runes/wards, illusory walls, and environmental chaos (lighting, space, reinforcements)**—it’s a magically trapped, perception-warping battlefield.\n\nKey Attributes  \n- Defenses (OBSERVED): **Runes along the walls activated when Caelynn cast her spell**, plus **ancient defensive wards** that affect the battle environment. These can trigger effects like the arcane trap bursts already impacting the Players (paralysis, force damage).  \n- Defenses (OBSERVED): **Illusory Walls** present in parts of the room, contributing to disorientation and mispositioning mid-fight.  \n- Geography (OBSERVED): **Large circular room with a central table and high, arched ceilings**—verticality and line-of-sight issues (e.g., hard to reach elevated targets). Also includes a **hidden trapdoor**, which can introduce threats or movement complications.  \n- Atmosphere (OBSERVED): **Almost the entire room is lit up by Fireball**, creating chaotic visibility and possibly obscuring hazards.  \n- Current Activity (CANON/OBSERVED blend): **Guards are being drawn here as reinforcements**, adding pressure over time.  \n\nNet effect: shifting terrain (illusions), reactive magic (runes/wards), and escalating pressure (reinforcements + chaotic visibility) all stack to disrupt positioning, targeting, and planning.", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 732, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 20, "top_5": [["ent_flesh_golem", 2.1943], ["ent_council_room", 1.8139], ["ent_city_council", 1.8064], ["ent_falling_debris", 1.7191], ["ent_the_city", 1.68]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_flesh_golem", "ent_council_room", "ent_city_council", "ent_falling_debris", "ent_the_city", "ent_grobnok_the_goblin", "ent_citys_rise_to_prominence", "ent_side_chamb