{"id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_4_v2", "question": "If the council keeps talking and doesn't act, what bites us?", "answer": "TL;DR: Delay lets **the cult** advance their plan—moving through hidden routes, exploiting council influence, and pushing toward summoning the flesh kaiju—while **the city** drifts closer to disaster with weakened coordination and defenses.\n\nIf the council stalls, the pressure points all worsen at once. **The cult** is already active beneath the city and using sewers/hidden infrastructure (CANON/OBSERVED). They can keep progressing toward “access the heart of the city” and “complete their summoning,” or pivot to sabotaging cauldrons and other systems if blocked (CANON). They also have **influence in the council**, so inaction may not be neutral—it can actively favor them (CANON).\n\nMeanwhile, **the city’s operational status** explicitly degrades: it is “brought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate,” with a **planned magical lockdown** not yet enacted and defenses already a concern (OBSERVED/CANON). Coordinated attacks across the city remain possible via hidden passages (CANON).\n\nFor the **players**, delay means lost initiative—they’re already “delayed by lengthy deliberation” and risk reacting instead of preventing.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Cult Goals: summon flesh kaiju; infiltrate via hidden routes; corrupt systems  \n- City Defenses: integrity in question; lockdown pending  \n- City Operational Status: worsening with inaction; threatened by cult  \n- Governance Risk: cult influence within council; indecision compounds danger", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 732, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 25, "top_5": [["ent_city_council", 2.06], ["ent_kaelyn", 1.5908], ["ent_persuasion_charisma", 1.5333], ["ent_convincing_the_council", 1.32], ["ent_citys_rise_to_prominence", 1.1495]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_city_council", "ent_kaelyn", "ent_persuasion_chari